<ui:UXML xmlns:ui="UnityEngine.UIElements" editor-extension-mode="False">
    <Style src="../Common/theme.uss" />
    <Style src="../CharacterRoster/character-roster.uss" />
    <Style src="../Common/tidbit.uss" />
    <!--
      DECK creation, as a SCENE. It made CHARACTERS until 2026-09-04; ADR-0009 deleted the
      container and the picker survived, because a deck's pairing is permanent and so "New Deck"
      opens on exactly this. The file, the scene and this folder still carry the old name — that
      is naming debt, not a second screen.

      It was three views inside a `.delete-modal` overlay in CharacterRosterScreen.uxml until
      2026-08-23. Same call the Store got on 2026-08-20 and for the same reason: it is
      full-screen, opaque and a destination, so the overlay was hosting rather than design.

      The three views are siblings, shown one at a time by CharacterCreateController. They keep
      their styling in character-roster.uss.

      THE PICKER HAS ART AGAIN (#312), AND STILL HAS NO SOLVER. What 7cc7c9f5 deleted was a
      WRAPPING grid whose portrait size was solved at runtime off GeometryChangedEvent — that is
      what NaN'd, thrashed and OOM-killed Android, not the presence of pictures. The shape here is
      two fixed columns of four plates, sized entirely by USS: no wrapping, no geometry callback,
      no per-element size write, nothing measured. Each plate is one Button carrying decorative
      children (`picking-mode="Ignore"`), so it is still ONE hit target per class.
      UxmlIntegrityCheck enforces the columns-and-no-grid boundary; keep it.
    -->
    <ui:VisualElement name="root" class="emb-root character-create-screen emb-bleed">

        <!-- PICKER: one plate per real class, fixed at four choices per column. The plates
             themselves are built in CharacterCreateController.BuildHeroChoice. -->
        <ui:VisualElement name="create-picker-view">
            <ui:VisualElement class="create-picker-header">
                <ui:VisualElement class="create-picker-header-spacer" />
                <ui:VisualElement class="create-picker-heading">
                    <ui:Label name="create-pass-title" text="Choose your hero" class="delete-title" />
                    <!-- THE ONLY PLACE THE PAIRING IS EXPLAINED BEFORE IT IS MADE (#312). A
                         character is two classes and the picker asks for them one at a time, so
                         without this line the second pass reads as "pick another hero" and the
                         player has no way to learn that the first pick is the one that decides the
                         Hero Power. Filled per pass by BuildHeroChoices. -->
                    <ui:Label name="create-pass-help" text="" class="create-pass-help" />
                </ui:VisualElement>
                <ui:Button name="create-cancel" text="Cancel" class="roster-button roster-button--ghost emb-back" />
            </ui:VisualElement>
            <ui:VisualElement name="create-hero-choices" class="hero-choice-list">
                <ui:VisualElement name="create-hero-column-left" class="hero-choice-column" />
                <ui:VisualElement name="create-hero-column-right" class="hero-choice-column" />
            </ui:VisualElement>
        </ui:VisualElement>

        <!-- DETAIL: a single hero's traits + hero power. The copy blocks are RESERVED BUT
             EMPTY (NOR-278): FlavorText and hero-power descriptions are unpopulated schema
             fields, and authoring that copy is out of scope. The layout space is held. -->
        <ui:VisualElement name="create-detail-view">
            <ui:VisualElement class="hero-detail-head">
                <ui:VisualElement name="create-detail-portrait" class="hero-detail-portrait" />
                <ui:VisualElement class="hero-detail-headings">
                    <ui:Label name="create-detail-name" text="" class="delete-title" />
                    <ui:Label name="create-detail-pass" text="" class="hero-detail-pass" />
                </ui:VisualElement>
            </ui:VisualElement>
            <ui:VisualElement name="create-detail-bullets" class="hero-detail-bullets" />
            <!-- The hero power block is filled from the class's HERO_POWER card (NOR-291):
                 the name is the card's own, the description is generated from its typed
                 rules, so it is the same text the power shows in a match and cannot drift
                 from what the power actually does. The caption is static. -->
            <ui:VisualElement name="create-power-block" class="hero-power-block">
                <ui:Label text="Hero Power" class="hero-power-caption" />
                <ui:Label name="create-power-name" text="" class="hero-power-name" />
                <ui:Label name="create-power-desc" text="" class="hero-power-desc" />
            </ui:VisualElement>
            <ui:VisualElement class="delete-actions">
                <ui:Button name="create-detail-back" text="Back" class="roster-button roster-button--ghost emb-back" />
                <ui:Button name="create-detail-select" text="Select" class="roster-button roster-button--cta" />
            </ui:VisualElement>
        </ui:VisualElement>

        <!-- CONFIRM: reached automatically once both classes are picked. It states the pairing,
             which is PERMANENT from the moment the deck exists (ADR-0009 ruling 1), and offers
             the two starter shapes. "Change something" drops the secondary pick only.

             THE NAME FIELD IS GONE (ADR-0009). It was here because a character's name was
             immutable and had to be settled at creation; a deck's is not, and the roster renames
             one from its own plate. It carried PlayerName.Check with it, which is not a loss:
             that predicate guards the DISPLAY NAME an opponent sees on the wire (VULN-002), and
             a deck name is never shown to anyone but its owner.

             There is no single "Create" here on purpose. The starter shape is the last decision
             and it is a fork, so it is two buttons rather than a control above one — the same
             call the deck dialog's own new-deck pane makes. RefreshConfirm hides Blank for the
             very first deck, which always gets a playable one. -->
        <ui:VisualElement name="create-confirm-view">
            <ui:Label text="Ready to build" class="delete-title" />
            <ui:Label name="create-confirm-summary" text="" class="create-help" />
            <ui:Label name="create-starter-note" text="" class="create-help create-help--starter" />
            <ui:Label name="create-error" text="" class="create-error" />
            <ui:VisualElement class="delete-actions">
                <ui:Button name="create-change" text="Wait!" class="roster-button roster-button--ghost" />
                <ui:Button name="create-blank" text="Start blank" class="roster-button roster-button--ghost" />
                <ui:Button name="create-generated" text="Generate a queue-ready deck" class="roster-button roster-button--cta" />
            </ui:VisualElement>
        </ui:VisualElement>

        <!-- TIDBIT: the first-run card, driven by FirstRunTidbit. LAST CHILD ON PURPOSE —
             UI Toolkit has no z-index, so document order is the only thing putting this over
             the three views. It starts hidden in the markup AND FirstRunTidbit hides it again
             in its constructor, because a backdrop left up is a screen the player cannot use.

             The tree is copied per host, the shape PackRevealPanel established: the panel
             queries `tidbit-*` out of whatever root it is handed, so a host styles the Got it
             control in its own screen's language without the panel knowing.

             NOTE FOR ANYONE EDITING THIS COMMENT: a doubled hyphen is illegal inside an XML
             comment and voids the whole document. Naming a BEM modifier class here is what
             does it, so refer to them in prose. It fails by emptying the screen. -->
        <ui:VisualElement name="tidbit-overlay" class="tidbit-overlay tidbit-overlay--hidden">
            <ui:VisualElement name="tidbit-card" class="tidbit-card">
                <ui:VisualElement class="tidbit-header">
                    <ui:Label name="tidbit-title" text="" class="tidbit-title" />
                </ui:VisualElement>
                <ui:VisualElement class="tidbit-body-row">
                    <!-- Hidden by FirstRunTidbit.Render until the art exists; see its
                         retirement trigger and spec §6.5, file 15. -->
                    <ui:VisualElement name="tidbit-art" class="tidbit-art" picking-mode="Ignore" />
                    <ui:Label name="tidbit-body" text="" class="tidbit-copy" />
                </ui:VisualElement>
                <ui:VisualElement class="tidbit-actions">
                    <ui:Button name="btn-tidbit-done" text="Got it" class="roster-button roster-button--cta" />
                </ui:VisualElement>
            </ui:VisualElement>
        </ui:VisualElement>

    </ui:VisualElement>
</ui:UXML>
